WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.736
This lesson becomes clearer when before the worked example, read charging and discharging as exponential processes controlled by the time constant.

2
00:00:07.736 --> 00:00:15.472
Charging means fast then slower: The capacitor voltage rises quickly at first and then approaches the supply more gently.

3
00:00:15.472 --> 00:00:23.208
Discharging means steep then flatter: The capacitor voltage falls quickly at first and then decays more slowly.

4
00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:30.944
Main controller means time constant: The product R C sets the characteristic response timescale of the circuit.

5
00:00:30.944 --> 00:00:38.680
RC behavior is a changing-rate process controlled by the time constant, not a straight-line fill or emptying.

6
